      "dcterms:title": "Verification steps",
      "dcterms:description": "The steps of DVC verification in the order they run (STT-VER-001), as the HCERT library names them in its typed result (STT-VER-008).",
      "dcterms:type": "Terminology: Code Systems",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/CodeSystem/TrustDemoVerificationStep"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "CodeSystem-TrustDemoVhlRefusalReason.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:CodeSystem",
      "dcterms:identifier": "CodeSystem/TrustDemoVhlRefusalReason",
      "dcterms:title": "Why a shared link released nothing",
      "dcterms:description": "The refusal reasons of decision table TD.DT.05 (STD-ACC-001).",
      "dcterms:type": "Terminology: Code Systems",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/CodeSystem/TrustDemoVhlRefusalReason"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ConceptMap-TrustDemoProductToLaoEpi.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:ConceptMap",
      "dcterms:identifier": "ConceptMap/TrustDemoProductToLaoEpi",
      "dcterms:title": "J3 map: vaccine product to national schedule dose",
      "dcterms:description": "The national map the clinic EHR uses in J3 to add the schedule code beside the issuer's product code, which it never replaces. The Hep B product had no entry until Nurse Chanthasone confirmed its equivalence on 2025-11-25 (see TrustDemoJ3Adjudication); her decision is recorded here so the next clinic need not make it again.",
      "dcterms:type": "Terminology: Concept Maps",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/ConceptMap/TrustDemoProductToLaoEpi"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdBirthDoseDvc.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdBirthDoseDvc",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J1 Birth-dose DVC",
      "dcterms:description": "What the birth hospital records for each birth dose and signs into one Digital Vaccination Certificate (DVC, an HCERT) per dose: the payload, the CWT claims and the key that signs it.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdBirthDoseDvc"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdChwReferral.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdChwReferral",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J2B Referral for verification",
      "dcterms:description": "The community health worker's referral of the child to the home clinic, to verify the foreign cards and fit the doses to the national schedule.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdChwReferral"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdChwRegistration.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdChwRegistration",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J2A Newborn registration on a home visit",
      "dcterms:description": "What the community health worker records offline when she finds a newborn missing from the household roster: the registration form's answers and each dose read from a foreign card without verifying it.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdChwRegistration"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdDvcVerification.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdDvcVerification",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J3A DVC verification and import",
      "dcterms:description": "What the clinic records when it verifies a foreign DVC against its cached copy of the trust list, and, when the DVC verifies, imports the dose in place of the reported one.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdDvcVerification"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdImportedDose.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdImportedDose",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J3B Imported dose and schedule",
      "dcterms:description": "What the clinic records for each imported dose's vaccine code, and what the national schedule finds due once the doses are counted.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdImportedDose"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdVhlAccess.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlAccess",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J41 Access to a shared link",
      "dcterms:description": "What the home country logs for every request to open a shared link, released or refused.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlAccess"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoDdVhlShare.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlShare",
      "dcterms:title": "TD.J40 Shared link and consent",
      "dcterms:description": "What the home country records when the holder shares a family member's summary as a Verifiable Health Link (VHL): who may read what, for how long, and that a passcode protects it.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoDdVhlShare"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoDvcVerification.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoDvcVerification",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: foreign DVC verified against the GDHCN trust list",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J3a. The district EHR verifies each Thai DVC offline against its cached copy of the GDHCN trust list, then imports the dose. This record says so.\n\nWhy: a verified dose replaces a reported one, so the record must show who verified what, against which policy, and which reported doses it removes. Anyone who later doubts a dose can follow this record back to the signed certificate and the issuing country's key.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoDvcVerification"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoHousehold.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoHousehold",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: household on the CHW's roster",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2a. The CHW finds that a newborn is missing from the household roster and adds Somsack as a member.\n\nWhy: Lao community health work is organized by household. The roster is how a CHW notices that a child is missing, and it is the unit the family phone shares under in J4 (one phone, three profiles).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoHousehold"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoImmunization.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: dose on the national schedule",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J3 and after. These are the Thai birth doses once the district clinic has verified them, and every dose given in Lao PDR.\n\nWhy: the Lao schedule engine works on Lao EPI codes, so each dose must carry one. A dose that came from abroad keeps the issuer's product code beside the Lao one, added through the ConceptMap and confirmed by the nurse. Nothing the other country said is overwritten. A verified foreign dose is recorded from its primary source, the signing hospital, and its Provenance says how it was verified.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoImmunization"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoPatient.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoPatient",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: child registered by the community health worker",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2 onwards. Vilay registers Somsack on a home visit, and the same patient carries every Lao record that follows: the verified Thai doses, the Lao doses and the summary shared in J4.\n\nWhy: a child born abroad is not in the Lao civil registry yet. A temporary id lets the CHW, the district clinic and the national portal all refer to the same child until civil registration catches up. The parents are recorded as contacts, because they hold the paper cards and later the family's VHLs.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoPatient"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoReferral.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoReferral",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: CHW referral to verify foreign cards",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2b. The CHW refers Somsack to the district health center to have his foreign cards verified and his doses fitted to the Lao schedule.\n\nWhy: the CHW cannot verify a DVC on the phone, but the clinic can. The referral points at the reported doses it is about, so the clinic knows exactly what to check, and the CHW can see when it is done.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoReferral"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoRegistration.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoRegistration",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: newborn registration captured offline",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2a. These are the CHW's answers on the newborn registration form, which the app renders with Structured Data Capture and saves with no signal.\n\nWhy: in Lao PDR the form is the configuration, not code. A ministry can change the questions without shipping a new app. The answers are kept so that the Patient and Group extracted from them can always be traced back to what was asked and who answered.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoRegistration"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoReportedImmunization.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoReportedImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: foreign dose as reported (not yet verified)",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J2b. The CHW app reads each Thai paper DVC offline without checking its signature, and saves the dose like this.\n\nWhy: a CHW phone may have no trust list and no signal, but the doses should not be lost. Recording them with primarySource false and the family as the information source keeps them visibly \"reported, not verified\". The schedule will not count them until a clinic verifies them (J3). Only the issuer's product code is present, because mapping to the Lao schedule is a clinical step for later.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoReportedImmunization"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoLaoVhlAccess.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoVhlAccess",
      "dcterms:title": "Lao PDR: every VHL access logged at home",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J4.1. The Lao national gateway records each attempt by a clinic abroad to fetch a family member's VHL manifest, the refused ones included.\n\nWhy: the family shares a link, not a copy, and the data stays in Lao PDR. Logging every access at home, following IHE Basic Audit Log Patterns, is what lets the family and the ministry see who looked, from where and when. A wrong passcode is logged too.",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoLaoVhlAccess"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoThImmunization.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThImmunization",
      "dcterms:title": "Thailand: dose given at the birth hospital (DVC source)",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J1. Each birth dose (Hep B, BCG) that Dr Anan gives is recorded here first. The hospital then packs it into a Digital Vaccination Certificate (HCERT, signed with XXR's key) and prints it as a QR card.\n\nWhy: the DVC can only carry what this record holds. The vaccine product, date, lot, dose number and the administering organization are exactly the fields the HCERT certificate needs. They are required here so every printed card is complete. The product is coded from the WHO PreQual-style product list, because that is the code Lao PDR will later map to its own schedule (J3).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThImmunization"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoThPatient.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThPatient",
      "dcterms:title": "Thailand: newborn at the birth hospital",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J1. Chiang Rai Provincial Hospital registers Somsack under its own hospital number on the day he is born.\n\nWhy: a baby born to Lao parents in Thailand has no Thai citizen id, so the hospital number is the only identifier the hospital can put behind the dose records it signs. The DVCs it prints carry the name and date of birth, not this number. The family's home country therefore cannot rely on any Thai identifier, and links the doses to its own patient (see the Lao patient profile).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThPatient"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDemoThVhlReceipt.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThVhlReceipt",
      "dcterms:title": "Thailand: record of a summary read through a VHL",
      "dcterms:description": "How it is used: J4.1. The Chiang Rai clinic viewer keeps this record when it opens Somsack's patient summary through the Verifiable Health Link that his father shows.\n\nWhy: the Thai clinic views the Lao record and does not copy it into a Thai registry. So the clinic keeps a note of what it saw, where it came from, and how it was verified: the VHL's signature against Lao PDR's key on the GDHCN trust list, the manifest fetch, and the passcode. The Lao side keeps its own log of the same access (the Lao audit profile).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Resource Profiles",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust-demo/StructureDefinition/TrustDemoThVhlReceipt"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "ValueSet-TrustDemoCodeMappingBasisVS.jsonld",
      "@type": "fhir:ValueSet",
